  "name": "Question 3",
  "problem": "Find a normal vector to the plane\n\n$$\nr=\u27e83,\\sqrt{7},-2\u27e9+t\u27e8-2,8,0\u27e9+s\u27e83,-1,-1\u27e9,\\,t,\\,s\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\n$$",
  "worked_solution": "From the parametric equation, we have that $v=\u27e8-2,8,0\u27e9$ and $w=\u27e83,-1,-1\u27e9$ are parallel to the plane.\n\nNow, we need to find a normal vector of the plane. To do that, we use the cross product of $v$ and $w$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}n & =v\\times w \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 8 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\\times [\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\left|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ -2 & 8 & 0 \\\\ 3 & -1 & -1\\end{aligned}\\right| \\\\  & =-8i-2j-22k \\\\  & =\u27e8-8,-2,-22\u27e9.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, a normal vector to the plane is $n=\u27e8-8,-2,-22\u27e9.$",
